A||||24||hyhy4u||Could I just maybe have a chance???||||3||
Z||000000||hyhy4u||06-07-2001||10:44 AM||||My bro in law just got his 1989 Ford Mustang GT started and theres talk of a race between his mustang and my 87 GT Fiero.  The only thing is he has the stock 5.0 V8 H.O. and I only got a 2.8 V6, I have driven it before and i gotta say that things got quite a bit of power, do ya think I could at least keep up with him??, lol, my cars stock except for a modified air system which i did which makes for more top end, tell me what you guys think, we will find out though in a few days if i can keep up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000001||AusFiero||06-07-2001||10:54 AM||||Better ask for a head start  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000002||hyhy4u||06-07-2001||10:57 AM||||Ha Ha, great...if theres nothing i hate more then looking at the rear end of a Ford during a race.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric||06-07-2001||10:58 AM||||If you race to 50mph, you may stay with him.  After 50, there will be no hope for you my friend.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||06-07-2001||10:59 AM||||If his is an automatic and yours is a stick shift. You have a chance to jump ahead off the line up to about 30-40mph. But once the the weight of the mustang get's moving the V-8 will pass you by at around 50mph. The late 80's mustang 5.0's had more HP than the first 5.0's. If his was an earlier 5.0 you'd have a better chance of at least staying close. So to answer you question, No. You may take him off the line but after that he's gone.<BR>With a stick shift Fiero you can stay door to door with a mid-80's 5.0 with auto trans up to 60-70mph. I think it was 87 or 88 when they increased the HP of the 5.0's. They increased HP when the F-body cars started getting the 350's.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||06-07-2001||11:03 AM||||If your Mustang-driving buddy can drive, you have no chance, my friend.<P>I drove a buddy's '89 5.0 LX 5-speed, bone stock, with a highway gear (2.76, maybe?).  The old ass-o-meter tells me it was about as fast as 87ECO5's Coupe w/3.4 swap, which is to say, quite a bit faster than a 2.8 Fiero.<P>Then my Mustang buddy went to a shorter rear gear (3-fifty-something), underdrive pulleys and removed his cats.  The gear made a HUGE difference...all of a sudden that Mustang was faster than hell.  Too bad he wound up crashing it into a dumpster.  <p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 06-07-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000006||Old Lar||06-07-2001||11:20 AM||||Lets see, you want to race a 5L Mustang with a 2.8L Fiero.  If he wins, he beats a car with a power plant about 1/2 the size of his Mustang.  No shame there for you or no big deal.<P>If you beat him he gets real humilation because a small V6 beats out a 5L V8.<P>Race him for the fun of it, No big deal if you lose, but real humiliation for him if you win or even keep close.||||reg||3
Z||000007||Steve Normington||06-07-2001||12:20 PM||||Challenge him to a slalom course, driver skill is much more important than HP.||||reg||1
Z||000008||hyhy4u||06-07-2001||01:17 PM||||Oh..yeah..you cant believe how many slalom courses there are here in the great plains of Illinois||||reg||10
Z||000009||stsmithgt||06-07-2001||01:34 PM||||Use a few pylons or get your friends to stand out there to slalom around. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000010||Ken Wittlief||06-07-2001||01:36 PM||||darn, i was just gonna say, if you can find a twisted mountain road with lots of 25mph S curves, then he has no chance,<P>  but now that I think of it, Ive been to illinois, you can get out on the highway and lock down the steering wheel, and you wont need to turn till you get halfway through Colarodo.<P>   You're only hope is 100' of steel cable, one end attached to his rear axle, the other around a tree. (ala American Grafitti)<P>   but he'll still have you for the first 99'||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||06-07-2001||01:41 PM||||I was out on lake ontario one sunny afternoon on my Hobiecat sailboat, flying a hull, trapped out, doing about 20mph, and some guys come buy on PWC's (jet skis) <P> while they are passing me one yells out, "hey! wanna race"<P>  I yelled back, "Ok - I'll race you to Toronto"<P>  Toronto is 90 miles from rocheseter across the lake. Jet skis have about a 40 to 50 mile range, and there is no place to refuel in the middle of lake ontario.<P>   sailboats have an infinite range (c:||||reg||1
Z||000012||84Bill||06-07-2001||01:41 PM||||You might have a chance if you poke him in the eyes before the race.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
