Z||000014||The Fieromaster||06-07-2001||01:55 PM||||Well i hav had my shortcummings racing stangs!  But ill tell you a stock 5.0L you can hang with to a certain point then he will eat you up... maybe not to 40 or so maybe 50 like said above!  It all depends on your car... Ive seen some FAST stock fieros and some SLOW stock Fieros!  It all depends wich yours is... But i wouldnt try against even a auto 4.6L I realized this weekend how fast they are when i watched a 4.6 (auto) eat a modified (intake, exhaust) 5.0GT (94? stick).. It was SAD!  Gotta love hommade off street drag strips!  The SNAKE crossing in Mentor!  It WILL be the Peg' crossing soon as James and I finish turbos!!  Right bro??<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">   <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000015||Oreif||06-07-2001||02:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hyhy4u:<BR><B>Oh..yeah..you cant believe how many slalom courses there are here in the great plains of Illinois</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey tell him you'll race him. Black Hawk Farms race course. Near Janesville Wisconsin.<BR>It's a 3/4 mile course and A bone stock Fiero can have way faster lap times than a V-8 stock Mustang. Even a 2.5L duke Fiero can get faster lap times! The longest straight way is only 1/8 mile and it's a HARD left at the end.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||TRiAD||06-07-2001||02:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hyhy4u:<BR><B>Oh..yeah..you cant believe how many slalom courses there are here in the great plains of Illinois</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Go to Utica IL (I-80 and I-39) on any given weekend, and bring money for an Autocross. There's almost always some club there racing, and most allow non-members.<P><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Toddster||06-07-2001||02:49 PM||||Don't despair! There is Hope. I was coming back from San Diego to LA one day 7 years ago (A LONG stretch of wide highway). A mid-80s Mustang came up and we raced for 50 miles. I was in my old Formula which had better handling in the light traffic but he only BARELY caught and passed me on the straight away. We both had BONE STOCK engines. If I had removed the water separater, ported the exhaust manifolds, put in low restirction cat and muffler, upped the ignition system, and put in a K&N filter (all simple and cheap mods), I have no doubt that I would have been able to keep pace with him on the straight away.<P>What have you got to lose but your dignity! Go 4 it!||||reg||1
