Z||000023||banditbalz||06-08-2001||07:40 PM||||5.0's came out with fuel injection in '86. FoMoCo artificially rated this setup at 225 hp. Motor in fact only produced 215 bhp. all 5.0's had 300 lbs/ft of torque. <BR>I have a friend with a modified 89 GT, 5 speed, Flowmaster exhaust, GT40 intake, Crane Cam. We raced several times (we both had our g/f with us) and I was always 4-6 car lengths ahead at 90km/h (50 mp/h). We both chirp our tires and connect right away. We took our racing to Cayuga Dragway Park where I posted a best of 15.2 to his best of 15.3 His trap speed was 92 mph to my 90 mph.<BR>I have another friend with a '95 Stang, 5.0 with a slushbox tranny and SVO side exhaust setup. This wasn't even a challenge. I thought maybe he got a bad launch, but after 3 kills, I decided to save my rubber for some real competition. <BR>I am not saying all mustangs are slow (I once lost a race in aprox. 35 street races with Mustangs), but rather they sound great and can be built to go fast for very little amount of money.<BR>Anyways, enough of my kill stories...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/launch_4.jpg">  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||14
Z||000024||pontiacs4me||06-09-2001||12:03 AM||||I have a friend with a 1986 gt mustang, heads I ported, a cobra intake, headers, no cats, flowmasters, 4.11 gears and a automatic od tranny, he has run best of 13.96 at 101.  I want my fiero to be in the low 13's when Im done.  I want vettes!||||reg||1
